aarch64 Objective-C dispatch: cast the messengers, and no stret variant.

On arm64 objc-api.h forces OBJC_OLD_DISPATCH_PROTOTYPES to 0 (the arm64 ABI
requires the dispatch functions to be called through a correctly-typed function
pointer -- variadic arguments go on the stack there, but the messenger trampoline
reads them from registers). These call sites were relying on the old uncast form,
so they fail to compile for arm64. Casting each objc_msgSend / objc_msgSendSuper /
method_invoke / stored IMP to its real signature is a no-op on x86 and correct on
both. Additionally method_invoke_stret is OBJC_ARM64_UNAVAILABLE: arm64 has no
separate struct-return messenger (the caller passes the indirect result pointer in
x8, which method_invoke preserves), so the value getters use method_invoke there.
